    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn reciprocal expressions and quadratic relations.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If x+1/x is known, square it:\n\n(x+1/x)^2 = x^2 + 2 + 1/x^2.\n\nSo x^2+1/x^2 = (x+1/x)^2 - 2.\n\nYou usually do not need to find x itself.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
